        "market_heading": "Why virtual staging matters in the Philadelphia real estate market",
        "market_text": "<p>The classic Philly rowhome is a home staging problem by design: a straight-through floor plan where the living room, dining space and kitchen blur together in photos. Staged furniture defines the zones, so buyers scrolling Zillow can read the layout in one glance instead of guessing where one room ends and the next begins.</p><p>Philadelphia's stock also runs old and narrow. Trinity houses, two-bedroom rowhomes and converted flats have proportions that empty photography flattens — a 12-foot-wide room reads as a corridor until there's furniture in it establishing scale.</p><p>The city's price range works in staging's favour too. On a rowhome listed well under the coastal-metro median, a month of physical staging is a meaningful percentage of the seller's net. Staging the photos instead keeps the marketing budget proportional to the sale.</p><p>97% of buyers use the internet in their home search (NAR), so Philadelphia agents compete on Zillow and Bright MLS photos long before a showing, and staged photos tend to draw more clicks and showing requests. Virtual staging shows a property's potential — rowhouses, condos and single family homes alike — at a fraction of the cost of traditional staging, with no delay waiting on a stager's truck and none of the logistics of moving furniture into a rowhome. Historic homes benefit most: period rooms read better once furniture shows how they work today.</p>",
        "local_heading": "Staged for every buyer in the Philadelphia market",
        "local_text": "<p>Designers stage contemporary for Fishtown and Northern Liberties, classic and period-aware for Society Hill and Rittenhouse, and practical family looks for the Main Line and the northwest neighbourhoods.</p><p>Narrow-room composition is the specialty here. Trinities and straight-through rowhomes get furniture chosen for scale first, so the photo proves the room works rather than just decorating it.</p><p>Tell us the target buyer and the designer tailors the style to them. Every image comes back Bright MLS-ready with disclosure guidance. Upload whenever you're ready; volume discounts apply automatically — 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+ — for investors and builders with several homes.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Where we stage most",
        "hoods": "Fishtown, Northern Liberties, Fairmount, Rittenhouse, Society Hill, Queen Village, Graduate Hospital, Manayunk, Chestnut Hill"
